{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds","id":1061403,"title":"5th Edition New Breeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-11T18:43:55-08:00","id":1061403,"title":"5th Edition New Breeds","content":"So here we go, with VTM 5th ED in the works that mean WtA is not far behind so to say. I am starting this thread to see what ideas we can come with. So new Breeds which it has been stated that Gaia can create new Breeds of Shifters if needed. So I going to set some ground rules for this thread. <br /> <br /> Rules: <br /> 1. Must be a total new breed. No new wolves/cats/snake etc...<br /> 2. Must have a job given by Gaia<br /> 3. Must have a vulnerability Gold/Silver/normal regeneration w/o rage etc....<br /> 4. Please include any special abilities such as gifts/forms/natural abilities","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:23:14-08:00","id":1061416,"title":"","content":"Koala's.<br /> The Imagination/Creativity of Gaia<br /> They have 3 forms. Their Crinos-equivalent is dreamed up similar to Mokole.<br /> Vulnerabilities to both Silver and Gold since they honor both Luna and Helios (they sleep so much, I can't see them being favored by one over the other).<br /> Not sure about any special abilities, as it's been a long time since I gave this any thought.<br /> <br /> I had once began planning on having Gaia distribute various aspects of her personality around the world. So her laughter (the Nuwisha) were tucked away in N.America. I hadn't gotten very far in the thought experiment to come up with others. Maybe Penguins for something since they're some of the only animals to be found around Antarctica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:46:05-08:00","id":1061418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061416#post1061416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Koala's.<br /> The Imagination/Creativity of Gaia<br /> They have 3 forms. Their Crinos-equivalent is dreamed up similar to Mokole.<br /> Vulnerabilities to both Silver and Gold since they honor both Luna and Helios (they sleep so much, I can't see them being favored by one over the other).<br /> Not sure about any special abilities, as it's been a long time since I gave this any thought.<br /> <br /> I had once began planning on having Gaia distribute various aspects of her personality around the world. So her laughter (the Nuwisha) were tucked away in N.America. I hadn't gotten very far in the thought experiment to come up with others. Maybe Penguins for something since they're some of the only animals to be found around Antarctica.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf favors dangerous carnivores, so you might want to go with leopard seals instead of penguins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:49:04-08:00","id":1061419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061416#post1061416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Koala's.<br /> The Imagination/Creativity of Gaia<br /> They have 3 forms. Their Crinos-equivalent is dreamed up similar to Mokole.<br /> Vulnerabilities to both Silver and Gold since they honor both Luna and Helios (they sleep so much, I can't see them being favored by one over the other).<br /> Not sure about any special abilities, as it's been a long time since I gave this any thought.<br /> <br /> I had once began planning on having Gaia distribute various aspects of her personality around the world. So her laughter (the Nuwisha) were tucked away in N.America. I hadn't gotten very far in the thought experiment to come up with others. Maybe Penguins for something since they're some of the only animals to be found around Antarctica.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See I have to agree with concepts like this because Australia would be missing a lot of the mammal breeds (Bears, Cats, Auroch, Boar, Nuwisha/Kitsune), and well Australian Garou are the only things covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T20:12:38-08:00","id":1061421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061418#post1061418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf favors dangerous carnivores, so you might want to go with leopard seals instead of penguins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Like I said, I hadn't gotten terribly far passed my idea for the Koalas. I just kind of planned on tucking a new Fera away on each continent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:25:28-08:00","id":1061441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061421#post1061421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Like I said, I hadn't gotten terribly far passed my idea for the Koalas. I just kind of planned on tucking a new Fera away on each continent.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drop_bear\" target=\"_blank\">It's dropbear time.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:31:53-08:00","id":1061444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061441#post1061441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drop_bear\" target=\"_blank\">It's dropbear time.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This came up on the old forums I think and that's where the idea started for me.<br /> <br /> But I didn't want them to have a &quot;standard&quot; crinos. And what with them being high all of the time, I though &quot;The imagination (or creativity) of Gaia fit&quot;. And having another Breed piece together their war form was appealing to me.<br /> <br /> And with them possibly being extinct (or close enough to it to not matter), that also helps with why no new Breeds have been created. Maybe their last big hurrah was the Kitsune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T03:04:09-07:00","id":1061483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds#post1061403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So new Breeds which it has been stated that Gaia can create new Breeds of Shifters if needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where has this been said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T03:57:25-07:00","id":1061500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061483#post1061483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where has this been said?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be directly stated in order for that to be how shifting breeds come about. It isn't like all shifting breeds were born at one time, they emerged as needed over eons. Supposedly the Ananasi are the sole survivors of an age when insectile and arachnid shifters ruled. Mokole were around before the mammalian changing breeds, and then circumstances in the Tellurian necessitated other types of werebeasts. The Kitsune only recently popped up... seems like there is lots of evidence for Gaia creating warriors/healers/whatever as need be. Perhaps, if she is given time, new beings suited to the age of the Apocalypse would arise...<br /> <br /> The Samsa have been hinted at interesting Cockroach as potential children... they are only a mockery breed, but I think the patron of the Glasswalkers can read the writing on the wall; Cockroach knows that the Apocalypse is going to be terrible. In the aftermath of the destruction, perhaps the evolutionary clock will be turned back... maybe arthropod shifters will be needed once again, replacing current dominant lifeforms who are rendered extinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-12-2017, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T04:03:23-07:00","id":1061502,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> I meant along along the lines of has white wolf stated that 5th ed will have a way to make your own fera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T10:51:02-07:00","id":1061572,"title":"","content":"I propose the Were-River-Dolphin of the Amazons, known as the <i>&quot;Encantado&quot;</i> by the locals.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encantado_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encantado_(mythology</a>)<br /> <br /> They would no doubt fill the roles that the Nuwisha Take in North America, as they are tricksters who come from a perfect under-river realm of never-ending joy, and come into our world to understand pain, sadness and imperfection. They reproduced by seducing people who stay out too close to the rivers at night by taking the guise of sexually alluring men/women. It would be safe to assume their culture is exclusively made up of Ragabash and/or Galliards.<br /> <br /> The one catch to spotting a potential Encantado: They cannot conceal the blowholes of their Cetacean Nature, and hence ALWAYS wear a hat in Homid form to conceal it.<br /> <br /> Their status as bogeymen of river dwelling Amazonian Cultures is so iconic that fear of going beside the rivers at night is a common local phobia to this day.<br /> <br /> Vulnerabilities? Due to lust/seduction/ hedonism being their second nature, they (similar to the Toreador of &quot;Vampire&quot;) would porbably need to spend willpower to resist any and all temptation to indulge in carnal/physical pleasures (be it music/art/gourmet food/alcohol/drugs/sex) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> How's that for a starting point? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 03-12-2017, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T10:56:10-07:00","id":1061573,"title":"","content":"Elephants - Gaias herolds <br /> Owls - Riddle masters <br /> Donkeys / Asses - Teachers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T11:16:24-07:00","id":1061576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061502#post1061502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> I meant along along the lines of has white wolf stated that 5th ed will have a way to make your own fera?</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't. This is just supposed to be a fun thought experiment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061572#post1061572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How's that for a starting point? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea of Dolphin Changers is a fun one. These sound a lot more like Changelings than Fera though.<br /> I think they should also have a distinct role, and not just be Nuwisha, but in the rivers of South America.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T17:39:35-07:00","id":1061659,"title":"","content":"How about letting the Encantado be the &quot;official&quot; Bards of Gaia? <br /> The Mokole remember the past. The Nuwisha teaches wisdom through painful and sarcastic humor.<br /> Dolphins articulate joy through intricate dance and elaborate song, and the Encantado hail from realms of Unending Joy.<br /> So why not let the Weredolphins be &quot;The Joy of Gaia&quot;, who give Her Children much-needed hope by reminding them the importance of Joy through music, song and dance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T23:29:04-07:00","id":1061738,"title":"","content":"Horses? Defenders of Gaia? Their Gifts would focus on detecting corruption and protecting the natural world from the corrupted until the other Fera deal with the corruption. Their Human Kinfolk have maintained ranches for 'feral' horses so that the wild Animal Kinfolk can hide in plain sight. They are also inexplicably fond of archery and are the source of the legends of centaurs, though their hybrid form is a two metric ton/4 meter tall humanoid horse that gains +6 Strength, +1 Dexterity, +6 Stamina, and +1 Perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T04:00:01-07:00","id":1061776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061738#post1061738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horses? Defenders of Gaia? Their Gifts would focus on detecting corruption and protecting the natural world from the corrupted until the other Fera deal with the corruption. Their Human Kinfolk have maintained ranches for 'feral' horses so that the wild Animal Kinfolk can hide in plain sight. They are also inexplicably fond of archery and are the source of the legends of centaurs, though their hybrid form is a two metric ton/4 meter tall humanoid horse that gains +6 Strength, +1 Dexterity, +6 Stamina, and +1 Perception.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would their Glabro forms have been what we now know as The Centaur? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T07:43:53-07:00","id":1061821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061738#post1061738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horses? Defenders of Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their Gifts would focus on detecting corruption and protecting the natural world from the corrupted until the other Fera deal with the corruption. Their Human Kinfolk have maintained ranches for 'feral' horses so that the wild Animal Kinfolk can hide in plain sight. They are also inexplicably fond of archery and are the source of the legends of centaurs, though their hybrid form is a two metric ton/4 meter tall humanoid horse that gains +6 Strength, +1 Dexterity, +6 Stamina, and +1 Perception. </div> </div> </div>Not even Gurahl, who get 16-20 feet tall in Crinos and weigh significantly more, get that high a boost, and they pay for it in Dexterity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:18:09-07:00","id":1061828,"title":"","content":"hmmmn werescorpions?<br /> <br /> sent by gaia as a token of her regards to humanity,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T10:44:33-07:00","id":1061877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061776#post1061776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Would their Glabro forms have been what we now know as The Centaur? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know, I think that would be more a special form given by a Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:16:25-07:00","id":1061911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061776#post1061776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would their Glabro forms have been what we now know as The Centaur? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061877#post1061877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I do not know, I think that would be more a special form given by a Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could always go the route of the Ananasi and give them 2 different war-type forms. It'd be interesting to see another Fera with that alternate form sequence.<br /> And agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, that stat spread is more than a bit ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Maybe do something like:<br /> &quot;Crinos&quot; (bipedal horse-man): Str+3/Dex+2/Stam+4<br /> Centaur: Str+2/Dex+3/Stam+4<br /> Horse: Str+2/Dex+1/Stam+3<br /> <br /> Also, they would logically have a way of doing Agg outside of using Gifts to enhance attacks. At least the Apis got a Gore attack. Horses don't really have anything of that category.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's worth saying that a while ago I rebalanced all of the Fera forms to give approximately the same total stat bonuses and for Crinos/Hipso I use 9 points as the standard, so that's what I would use when making up new Fera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:36:40-07:00","id":1061919,"title":"","content":"Horses are much more powerful than White Wolf gives them credit for, so I think that the Hybrid and Equine forms would be much more powerful than people give them credit. Large horses are much stronger than any large carnivore like a bear, large horses can kill humans with a single kick if they are feeling hateful, so large horses should probably be considered to have a Strength 8. The only large carnivore that is as powerful as a large horse is a tiger, which is why carnivores tend to go after injured or sick horses because they do not want to get injured or killed.<br /> <br /> Two war forms would be interesting. You could have a homid, hybrid, centaur, and equine form. I would make the Hybrid form at Strength+6/Dexterity+1/Stamina+6/Perception+1, Centaur form at Strength+3/Dexterity+1/Stamina+3/Double Movement/Two Homid Hands, Equine form at Strength+4/Dexterity+1/Stamina+4/Perception+1/Double Movement. Since the Equine Fera would have no natural weapons, they would have no inherent way of dealing aggravated damage with their unarmed attacks (though they would deal lethal damage with their unarmed attacks). Unlike the Garou, who are the Warriors of Gaia, they would be the Defenders of Gaia and would focus around Gifts that enhance defense, detection, and mobility, and I would suggest that their Rage be similar to the Gurahl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:29:02-07:00","id":1061954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061919#post1061919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horses are much more powerful than White Wolf gives them credit for, so I think that the Hybrid and Equine forms would be much more powerful than people give them credit. Large horses are much stronger than any large carnivore like a bear, large horses can kill humans with a single kick if they are feeling hateful, so large horses should probably be considered to have a Strength 8. The only large carnivore that is as powerful as a large horse is a tiger, which is why carnivores tend to go after injured or sick horses because they do not want to get injured or killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but do you really want a bunch of kickboxing horses? I kinda like the idea of centaur-shifters, but the horse is seen as a symbol of many things- and being a scary threat to humans isn't one of them. Regardless of what a horse is physiologically capable of doing, it doesn't have the same primal image as a wolf, lion, or bear. I would not make them fighters/protectors. I think a role similar to the centaurs of myth would be interesting, offering counsel and wisdom. Perhaps (given the horse's speed) they could have been liaisons to the far-off Planetary Incarna, rarely ferrying those summoned before the Incarna to and fro. Maybe that is how humans garbled things and tied them to astrology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-13-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:55:12-07:00","id":1061970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061919#post1061919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Horses are much more powerful than White Wolf gives them credit for, so I think that the Hybrid and Equine forms would be much more powerful than people give them credit. Large horses are much stronger than any large carnivore like a bear, large horses can kill humans with a single kick if they are feeling hateful, so large horses should probably be considered to have a Strength 8. The only large carnivore that is as powerful as a large horse is a tiger, which is why carnivores tend to go after injured or sick horses because they do not want to get injured or killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just not how stats work in WoD though. If you want the larger horses to have a Str of 8, that would have the smaller ones with 7 and giving them +3 Str in Equine form covers that. You can even have the heavier horses get an extra +1 to Str at the cost of a +1 to Dex.<br /> <br /> And it's worth adding that the only reason Garou get +4 Str in Crinos is because of their divine roles as Warriors, not because wolves are inherently strong. The Fera's purpose plays a lot into the form bonuses (and abilities) it gets once its outside of Homid and Animal forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061919#post1061919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two war forms would be interesting. You could have a homid, hybrid, centaur, and equine form. I would make the Hybrid form at Strength+6/Dexterity+1/Stamina+6/Perception+1, Centaur form at Strength+3/Dexterity+1/Stamina+3/Double Movement/Two Homid Hands, Equine form at Strength+4/Dexterity+1/Stamina+4/Perception+1/Double Movement. Since the Equine Fera would have no natural weapons, they would have no inherent way of dealing aggravated damage with their unarmed attacks (though they would deal lethal damage with their unarmed attacks). Unlike the Garou, who are the Warriors of Gaia, they would be the Defenders of Gaia and would focus around Gifts that enhance defense, detection, and mobility, and I would suggest that their Rage be similar to the Gurahl.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are giving +14 to stats in hybrid form, which is completely out of line with how war forms are built. By your logic, the Gurahl Crinos should get +12 Strength and Stamina or so, given their how large they are. But since that is represented with a +5, you have to use that sort of balancing mechanism to build other Fera war forms as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061954#post1061954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but do you really want a bunch of kickboxing horses? I kinda like the idea of centaur-shifters, but the horse is seen as a symbol of many things- and being a scary threat to humans isn't one of them. Regardless of what a horse is physiologically capable of doing, it doesn't have the same primal image as a wolf, lion, or bear. I would not make them fighters/protectors. I think a role similar to the centaurs of myth would be interesting, offering counsel and wisdom. Perhaps (given the horse's speed) they could have been liaisons to the far-off Planetary Incarna, rarely ferrying those summoned before the Incarna to and fro. Maybe that is how humans garbled things and tied them to astrology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like this concept for their purpose. It works well without having them be off-brand warriors of Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-13-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T14:13:26-07:00","id":1061980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061970#post1061970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really like this concept for their purpose. It works well without having them be off-brand warriors of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, thanks- I went and re-read a bit on centaur myth, and it seems like I was sort of confusing the majority of the race with Chiron, who was basically a genius among centaurs due to him be the spawn of the Titan Cronus. Most centaurs are kind of like Bacchanalian satyrs, loutish savages who drink, carouse and break stuff. In that light, them being strong and even dangerous makes sense... but I would rather present that physical strength as much of a stumbling block as a source of power.<br /> <br /> I figure, why not have the horse fera be both brigands and teachers? Kinda like how Garou are both Gaia's noble protectors as well as bloody-minded monsters; maybe at their best, the horse-folk were wise instructors, passing on guidance gleaned from the great Incarna, and acting more as facilitators than simple messengers. Others, however, got too used to their positions of honor as the representatives to the 'higher' spirit courts, and abused their positions of influence and power. Eventually the instructors and diplomats were outnumbered by self-important dictators. These brutes were too enamored of their own lofty calling to <i>actually carry out </i>said calling, and instead found it easier to intimidate and order about those fera and kin weaker and slower than themselves.<br /> <br /> As far as names go, I kinda like just stealing the old progenitor king's name from the Greek myth, <i>Ixion</i>, and using that as a name for the horse-shifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-13-2017, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:10:20-07:00","id":1062010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061980#post1061980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hey, thanks- I went and re-read a bit on centaur myth, and it seems like I was sort of confusing the majority of the race with Chiron, who was basically a genius among centaurs due to him be the spawn of the Titan Cronus. Most centaurs are kind of like Bacchanalian satyrs, loutish savages who drink, carouse and break stuff. In that light, them being strong and even dangerous makes sense... but I would rather present that physical strength as much of a stumbling block as a source of power.<br /> <br /> I figure, why not have the horse fera be both brigands and teachers? Kinda like how Garou are both Gaia's noble protectors as well as bloody-minded monsters; maybe at their best, the horse-folk were wise instructors, passing on guidance gleaned from the great Incarna, and acting more as facilitators than simple messengers. Others, however, got too used to their positions of honor as the representatives to the 'higher' spirit courts, and abused their positions of influence and power. Eventually the instructors and diplomats were outnumbered by self-important dictators. These brutes were too enamored of their own lofty calling to <i>actually carry out </i>said calling, and instead found it easier to intimidate and order about those fera and kin weaker and slower than themselves.<br /> <br /> As far as names go, I kinda like just stealing the old progenitor king's name from the Greek myth, <i>Ixion</i>, and using that as a name for the horse-shifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So <u>Ixion</u> (Horse Shifters):<br /> (copying from above, 3 forms)<br /> Equiceph (bipedal horse-man, name taken from a D&amp;D race): Str+3/Dex+2/Stam+4<br /> Centaur: Str+2/Dex+3/Stam+4<br /> Horse: Str+2/Dex+1/Stam+3<br /> maybe drop 1 from Dex to put into Str to represent heavier horse breeds.<br /> No Metis, Starting Rage/Gnosis:<br /> Homid: 4/2<br /> Equine: 2/4<br /> Willpower: 4<br /> <br /> I think having them spend Rage like Gurahl is more interesting than extra actions (and could account for impressive feats of strength which could account for some of the brutish personification).<br /> Their role would be as Gaia's diplomats to the other Celestial Incarna (a role not really filled already) and so their Gifts can center around speed, endurance, archery and Umbral travel.<br /> For simplicity's sake I would just give them a General Gift list and then Breed Gifts and not worry about any sort of Auspice type list. Doing it that way would make it easier to compile.<br /> <br /> For weaknesses I'm not sure. I'm inclined to say that they should have both (Silver and Gold) or neither. It might be interesting to have a Breed that doesn't have a weakness, but still has Rage. Then again that goes against the general format so maybe not.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-13-2017, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:21:37-07:00","id":1062018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062010#post1062010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So <u>Ixion</u> (Horse Shifters):<br /> (copying from above, 3 forms)<br /> Equiceph (bipedal horse-man, name taken from a D&amp;D race): Str+3/Dex+2/Stam+4<br /> Centaur: Str+2/Dex+3/Stam+4<br /> Horse: Str+2/Dex+1/Stam+3<br /> maybe drop 1 from Dex to put into Str to represent heavier horse breeds.<br /> No Metis, Starting Rage/Gnosis:<br /> Homid: 4/2<br /> Equine: 2/4<br /> Willpower: 4<br /> <br /> I think having them spend Rage like Gurahl is more interesting than extra actions (and could account for impressive feats of strength which could account for some of the brutish personification).<br /> Their role would be as Gaia's diplomats to the other Celestial Incarna (a role not really filled already) and so their Gifts can center around speed, endurance, archery and Umbral travel.<br /> <br /> For weaknesses I'm not sure. I'm inclined to say that they should have both (Silver and Gold) or neither. It might be interesting to have a Breed that doesn't have a weakness, but still has Rage. Then again that goes against the general format so maybe not.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, a lot! I think using their Rage like Gurahl is a good idea. I think they could also be particularly good at running long distances. I mean, they're horses, duh, but I am talking about really long runs, like, to the moon and back sort of runs without too much difficulty. Running into the deepest parts of the umbra without needing anchorheads and such would be a cool trick, but that could easily be a gift rather than an innate ability.<br /> <br /> Depending on the time frame of their existence, they might not have earned any enmity from the Celestial Incarna, so perhaps they would not have any weaknesses.<br /> Alternatively, after they fail in their duties wholesale, perhaps they are cursed by both Helios and Luna.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:28:48-07:00","id":1062023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1061919#post1061919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horses are much more powerful than White Wolf gives them credit for, so I think that the Hybrid and Equine forms would be much more powerful than people give them credit. Large horses are much stronger than any large carnivore like a bear, large horses can kill humans with a single kick if they are feeling hateful, so large horses should probably be considered to have a Strength 8. The only large carnivore that is as powerful as a large horse is a tiger, which is why carnivores tend to go after injured or sick horses because they do not want to get injured or killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans have also lived through lots of horse kicks, in prehistory and modern times. It's not something you want to chance, to be certain, but also not an instant death sentence, else no one would have bothered trying to ride horses in the first place.<br /> <br /> As another matter, one of the most important things to realize about Crinos is that it often has jack-all to do with the actual size of the beast in question. Wolves are a hell of a lot less massive and powerful than just about anything, but werewolves in war form are several hundred pounds, nine feet tall, and have claws the size of long knives. They are so large that riding on horseback requires a separate Gift (Arion's Burden) to make it possible. Even rats and ravens get Strength boosts in their war forms. Mokole who turn into gila monsters can change into 2014 Godzilla. Gurahl Crinos is only slightly stronger than Garou Crinos. The list of unexpected weridness goes on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two war forms would be interesting. You could have a homid, hybrid, centaur, and equine form. I would make the Hybrid form at Strength+6/Dexterity+1/Stamina+6/Perception+1, Centaur form at Strength+3/Dexterity+1/Stamina+3/Double Movement/Two Homid Hands, Equine form at Strength+4/Dexterity+1/Stamina+4/Perception+1/Double Movement. </div> </div> </div>No way is something that large getting a positive Dexterity bonus. I don't even think that Khan and Simba Bastet should have positive Dexterity modifiers in their forms; fuckers are ten feet tall in Crinos and several hundred pounds across every form but Homid. Most of their high numbers probably have something to do with Satyr Brucato really liking werecats and pumping their stats up whenever possible (see also: WoD: Changing Breeds, for the Chronicles of Darkness; he developed the book and likely wrote a good bit for it, and the weretiger war forms are as strong and durable as elephants, only with higher Dexterity).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the Equine Fera would have no natural weapons, they would have no inherent way of dealing aggravated damage with their unarmed attacks (though they would deal lethal damage with their unarmed attacks). </div> </div> </div>Even rats and spiders can deal aggravated damage, so you may need to re-evaluate this position. Or conceptualize them as a type of (dons sunglasses) horseplaying gorgon instead of a type of Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlike the Garou, who are the Warriors of Gaia, they would be the Defenders of Gaia and would focus around Gifts that enhance defense, detection, and mobility, and I would suggest that their Rage be similar to the Gurahl. </div> </div> </div>Those are still all things that Garou still have to do. Gaia probably wouldn't give another breed that task unless the wolves died off completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:32:06-07:00","id":1062025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062018#post1062018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, a lot! I think using their Rage like Gurahl is a good idea. I think they could also be particularly good at running long distances. I mean, they're horses, duh, but I am talking about really long runs, like, to the moon and back sort of runs without too much difficulty. Running into the deepest parts of the umbra without needing anchorheads and such would be a cool trick, but that could easily be a gift rather than an innate ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Strider Gift, Tireless Running which could be a General Rank 1 Gift. It would let them long run while only making checks every 24 hours. Through the Umbra, that should be enough to get to the moon no problem. And if they had a Gift to provide sustenance by spending Gnosis (there is one, but I forgot where), that should allow them to run to the other planets and back (especially with things like Speed of Thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062018#post1062018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the time frame of their existence, they might not have earned any enmity from the Celestial Incarna, so perhaps they would not have any weaknesses.<br /> Alternatively, after they fail in their duties wholesale, perhaps they are cursed by both Helios and Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is along the lines of what I was thinking. Just wasn't sure how well it would be received since it does go against how the Fera in general are set up atm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T16:00:00-07:00","id":1062039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062010#post1062010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think having them spend Rage like Gurahl is more interesting than extra actions (and could account for impressive feats of strength which could account for some of the brutish personification).<br /> Their role would be as Gaia's diplomats to the other Celestial Incarna</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the planetary Incarnae? Gaia is a bit above that rank, so &quot;other&quot; is not the best term, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T16:13:44-07:00","id":1062047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062039#post1062039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean the planetary Incarnae? Gaia is a bit above that rank, so &quot;other&quot; is not the best term, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? All this stuff is said and your only input is a semantic quibble? :P C'mon, you can do better than that, Saur!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T17:16:39-07:00","id":1062076,"title":"","content":"I am confused about the idea of balance between the Fera breeds. There is no balance between the Fera breeds. Heck, there is no balance between the Bastet Tribes, and they belong to the same breed of Fera.<br /> <br /> Fera who are associated with larger animals tend to be stronger and tougher than Fera who are associated with smaller animals. Brown bears tend to average around 220 kilograms for males and 180 kilograms for females. Draft horses tend to average four times the mass of brown bears. I do not think that it would be odd for horse Fera to be stronger and tougher than bear Fera because horses are stronger and tougher than bears (Elephant Fera would be even stronger and tougher, I would think that their Crinos form would easily have Strength+10, Dexterity-1, Stamina+10, and Perception+1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T17:57:45-07:00","id":1062101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062039#post1062039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean the planetary Incarnae? Gaia is a bit above that rank, so &quot;other&quot; is not the best term, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the nitpick. I was worried about the terminology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Honestly, I think this role is better served by actual spirits, but this was someone else's idea and I was trying to expand upon it enough to be useful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062076#post1062076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am confused about the idea of balance between the Fera breeds. There is no balance between the Fera breeds. Heck, there is no balance between the Bastet Tribes, and they belong to the same breed of Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is debatable. But either way, I had stated that I purposefully set out to have them balanced, and I personally keep that in mind whenever statting out a new idea for a Changing Breed. There is little reason not to. If you set out to purposefully make something unbalanced then it is either inherently more fun or less fun for the players involved (imo).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062076#post1062076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fera who are associated with larger animals tend to be stronger and tougher than Fera who are associated with smaller animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please explain why Garou Crinos and Hispo are as strong as they are, considering how relatively weak wolves are to most of the Fera animal breeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062076#post1062076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Brown bears tend to average around 220 kilograms for males and 180 kilograms for females. Draft horses tend to average four times the mass of brown bears. I do not think that it would be odd for horse Fera to be stronger and tougher than bear Fera because horses are stronger and tougher than bears (Elephant Fera would be even stronger and tougher, I would think that their Crinos form would easily have Strength+10, Dexterity-1, Stamina+10, and Perception+1).</div> </div> </div> </div>First, why do you keep adding Perception to everything?<br /> Second, (again) Garou have +4 which is only 1 point less than Gurahl and Mokole who have 2-5 times the mass or more. The animal breed only had a little to do with what stats the Crinos form gets. It has a lot more to do with their assigned role and metaphysical aspects of the lore. As pointed out, rats and ravens (and Nagah and Nuwisha too) get a bonus even though their animal forms are pathetic. A Mokole Archid (even without huge size silliness) is going to be much larger than a Crinos horse. And they get +5. Now you can argue that they should have a lot more I suppose. But then you are setting about to redo all of the Fera's form stats to conform to your own expectations (I did just that a few years ago, and I still use those stats).<br /> In any case, I think spending Rage on Str should close any gaps for the Str expectations of their Crinos. I see no reason for a horse Crinos to have a possible base Str of 11 when 18' bears and literal Dragons top out at 10.<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, and for horses, I tend to view their bulk as adding more to Stamina than Strength which is why I was plotting the stats out the way I did. By all means, drop the Dex bonus entirely and just give them Strength and Stamina, and then they end up basically being horse shaped Gurahl stat-wise.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-13-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T03:17:34-07:00","id":1062216,"title":"","content":"Righto, keeping the Train of Thought of The <b> <i>&quot;Encantado&quot;</i> Weredolphins</b> Running before the caffeine in my blood runs dry.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Joy Of Gaia&quot;, who remind the world the importance of Joy and Hope through Music, Art, Song and Dance.<br /> <br /> Gregarious, Fun Loving and Lusty to a Fault, They Reproduce by seducing beautiful/charismatic/intelligent/morally-upstanding humans at riversides, often during celebrations. Hence Encantado have Homid-Kinfolk that run the whole-gamut of human races.<br /> The ONE dead-giveaway to their true nature; in all-forms, Encantado have a blowhole that can only be concealed by hats and long-hair.<br /> <br /> Going to use the Amazonian (based on actual real-world mythology) Encantado as the &quot;base&quot; of this Fera, with cultural variations.<br /> <br /> Edit: &quot;Encantado&quot; literally means &quot;Enchanted Ones&quot; in Brazilian Portuguese.<br /> <br /> <b>Sub-Species (Temporary &quot;Working Titles&quot; so far)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Amazonian Weredolphins (Encantado) :</b> The Most Famous and Well Known &quot;Face&quot; of this race. Gregarious and promiscuous to a fault, they also act as the &quot;bogeyman&quot; of the Amazon, teaching children to stay home at night, eat their vegetables, etc etc as well as spread music joy and dance.<br /> <br /> <b>Yangtzee Weredophins (Her-Twen):</b> Chinese River Weredolphins, who also act as emissaries of the Zhong-Long Were-Dragons of said waterways. Lovers of Poetry, Caligraphy, Wine and Harp Music. Though still greagarious, they also act as the ruthless &quot;judges&quot; of Chinese Waterways, drowning scoundrels and those of poor moral character, giving rise to the myth of &quot;Shui Gui&quot; (Water Ghosts) who pull drowning fishermen and those who stray too far into the water to their doom.<br /> <br /> <b>Ganges Weredolphin of India:</b> Sharing the poor eyesight of their Cetacean Kin, The Weredolphins of India take pride in their ancestor's mythological role of having borne the goddess Ganesha upon their backs whenever she traversed the Ganges River; due to their close history with the Indian Divine Courts, they fancy themselves closest to the spiritual world and are the self-proclaimed Theurges of the Encantado Fera. Has strong influence in the Bollywood Film Industry, as it promotes the Dance, Music and Romanticism much beloved by their culture. Considered haughty/arrogant by other Encantado as a rule.<br /> <br /> <b>Bottlenose Dolphin Encantado of the Sea (Manatee):</b> The most kind-hearted of the Encantado Race, the Were Ocean-Dolphins are the joyful and hopeful Yang to the vicious and cynical Ying of the Rokea, on whom they are on VERY poor terms with, much like their real-life Animal Counterparts. And yes, it is actually they who gave rise to legends of the the Mythical Manatee (not the real life Dougon) who rescue drowning sailors, share a season of love which results in a child, before returning said sailor to humanity forgetful and heartbroken.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Encantado Traits.</b><br /> Able to Hold Breath For MUCH longer than any other Air-Breathing Fera in ALL Forms (Homid: 5XStamina Minutes, Crinos 10X Stamina Minutes, Cetacean 20X Stamina Minutes)<br /> <br /> ALL Encantado have a blowhole in every-form, concealable only by hats and long hair.<br /> <br /> Encantado are capable of substituting sight with Sonar Echo Location in Glabro, Crinos, Hispo and Cetacean Forms), which also counts as the &quot;Racial Language&quot; which they and only they can speak and understand.<br /> <br /> And Naturally ALL Enacantado are born expert swimmers.<br /> <br /> Encantado must roll willpower to resist indulging in an activity of pleasure (Music/Dance/Alcohol/Partying/Sex/Love/Poetry/Art/Movies, ETC)<br /> <br /> Naturally Encantado &quot;Step Sideways&quot; Through Water, but instead of staring into it, sing/performs music to do so.<br /> <br /> Will work on stats later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thoughts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 03-14-2017, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T06:02:43-07:00","id":1062255,"title":"","content":"The problem with Cetecea Fera is that they already have a place within cWoD as Kami. Now, I could see dolphins being entire species of Kami, but I do not know if they would make good Fera. As for a blowhole in every form, that would make them physiologically more inhuman than the Ananasi because the blowhole would have to pass through their brain (which would also horribly compromise the structural integrity of their skull).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T06:22:45-07:00","id":1062261,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall way back when that Ethan Skemp said that the biggest problem with were-dolphins is that the species is rather sexually aggressive and this brought up a whole host of issues he didn't want to ever have to deal with. That said, the above idea is pretty cool. <br /> <br /> I, personally, want were-snails. Gaia's original messengers, until their failure to stop the first war of rage led to the job going to the Corax. <br /> <br /> (In all seriousness, as much as I enjoy all of the existing breeds, I would've preferred only having wolves, tigers, leopards, jaguars, hyena and sharks.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:16:14-07:00","id":1062278,"title":"","content":"I think that if I were to actually ever run a game of WTA (instead of just using WTA Lore and Concepts in my Sorcerer and Vampire games) I would completely overhaul which Breeds do what so that it makes sense from the ground up. Every single breed wasn't made all at once with a purpose in mind, the game evolved over time and new Breeds were added and they all needed new jobs. For example, I simply cannot see the purpose of Werehyenas, since they do something that nature does by itself already. Hyenas eat diseased babies (human or otherwise) who are left out on the plains as is, they don't need a Crinos form to get that job done.<br /> <br /> A Breed should only exist if there is a genuine need for it which cannot be fulfilled by regular nature.<br /> <br /> OR, alternatively, each Breed being given a purpose by Gaia is just lore that the Breeds made up as part of their religions and various cults, and they're just a spiritual phenomena which exists without any divine purpose... which would explain why the Lore has gaps and holes in it (for example, some important roles seem to only be carried out in some parts of the world) but this would also be an unfulfilling twist for a Werewolf game unless you were trying to promote nihilism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:20:59-07:00","id":1062282,"title":"","content":"As for a Breed I'd be interested in seeing...<br /> <br /> Werebirds. I feel like Corax are a tad restrictive, and it would be nice if they got a Bastet treatment and you could be a Falcon, Eagle, Owl, all with slight shifts in purpose. All of them are messengers, but get slightly different Forms and Gifts. So only Ravens get the Eye-Eating power, but Falcons get some combat powers from the Garou lists and Owls get some healing powers from the Gurahl lists. It would also make the Messengers global, since Ravens aren't a 100% globalized species but &quot;birds&quot; are.<br /> <br /> Wereinsects are something I want to want, but cannot actually see being cool. Werespiders are enough, and I'm glad that the Werebees were hounded to extinction in the Insect War.<br /> <br /> Wereapes is something that will never work since humans are so close to Apes as is. Same issue with Monkeys and other &quot;close&quot; relatives, since the point of Werewolf is being kin to something distinctly inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:32:15-07:00","id":1062288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062216#post1062216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's much closer to a standard Fera. I like it.<br /> For roles, how is the Joy of Gaia different from the Laughter of Gaia?<br /> <br /> On forms, I would drop the blowhole in homid, since Homid form is literally just supposed to be human form. I don't know that they need a Glabro, but if you give them one I would start with the blowhole concept there. And since that's a near human form, you can have the blowhole between the shoulder blades so as to not deal with the idea that there's an airway going up through the head of a mostly humanoid form.<br /> <br /> And while yes, cetaceans already have a role in the WoD as Rorqual, you could always try and say that those are just the larger ones and have dolphins be their own thing. The premise of this thread goes against canon anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062261#post1062261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall way back when that Ethan Skemp said that the biggest problem with were-dolphins is that the species is rather sexually aggressive and this brought up a whole host of issues he didn't want to ever have to deal with. That said, the above idea is pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn't heard that. Kind of funny that they then went and made Rokea fairly sexually aggressive once they come on land.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:48:23-07:00","id":1062295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062278#post1062278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if I were to actually ever run a game of WTA (instead of just using WTA Lore and Concepts in my Sorcerer and Vampire games) I would completely overhaul which Breeds do what so that it makes sense from the ground up. Every single breed wasn't made all at once with a purpose in mind, the game evolved over time and new Breeds were added and they all needed new jobs. For example, I simply cannot see the purpose of Werehyenas, since they do something that nature does by itself already. Hyenas eat diseased babies (human or otherwise) who are left out on the plains as is, they don't need a Crinos form to get that job done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hyenas under the Rainmakers purpose are meant to eat animals who have gone beyond deprivation, including but certainly not limited to humans. Hyenas under the Revised setting setup have basically the same purpose as the Garou. W20 moved back to the former because of the discovery that golden jackals are, in fact, a type of wolf, but their Gifts suggest a capability to deal with the dead that's more common than among Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As for a Breed I'd be interested in seeing...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Werebirds. I feel like Corax are a tad restrictive, and it would be nice if they got a Bastet treatment and you could be a Falcon, Eagle, Owl, all with slight shifts in purpose. All of them are messengers, but get slightly different Forms and Gifts. So only Ravens get the Eye-Eating power, but Falcons get some combat powers from the Garou lists and Owls get some healing powers from the Gurahl lists. It would also make the Messengers global, since Ravens aren't a 100% globalized species but &quot;birds&quot; are.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> They wouldn't be so near unified in purpose, if at all, especially given the bent of folklore matchups regarding different birds; owls, for instance, would not be healers, but psychopomps who communicate with the dead. I think I can recall that a number of birds of prey would actually fall under that category along with the owls, given an old, old discussion of hypothetical eagle changers on the early 00s-era WW boards (back when there was a different page for each message!). Also, given that Corax are actually a huge body of related corvids rather than just ravens proper, they actually cover a far, far greater territory that is close to worldwide, if not there already. Obviously, Antarctica remains rather inaccessible.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:55:10-07:00","id":1062300,"title":"","content":"Wow, I didn't know about other Corvids being Corax. Well in that case the Corax cover most of the world, apart from a good bit of South America. A simple fix is to simply change the setting so that some Corvids from the northern part of SA are also in the southern part. That means that there's no real need for the Werebats, and they can either be removed or get a new purpose. Werebats could simply be a relative of the Ratkin, with the same purpose but for areas which rats struggle to access.<br /> <br /> Well then, I would introduce a new Bird Breed which was a large family of carnivorous birds who were Gaia's Warriors for the Sky. We have Land Warriors, Sea Warriors, and these would be Sky Warriors. More frail than Garou, (lacking Stamina boosts and soak-related gifts) but with greater Dexterity. Can someone who is into animal taxonomy give a good overarching family similar to Corvids which captures meat-eating, aggressive birds? It doesn't HAVE to be scientific in terms of taxonomy, but that would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-14-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:59:30-07:00","id":1062301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062278#post1062278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every single breed wasn't made all at once with a purpose in mind, the game evolved over time and new Breeds were added and they all needed new jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh. most or all of the breeds were put out at the same time (Player's Handbook). The Breed books later on just vastly expanded on each (except for the Nuwisha one that got a horribly short page count).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062278#post1062278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For example, I simply cannot see the purpose of Werehyenas, since they do something that nature does by itself already. Hyenas eat diseased babies (human or otherwise) who are left out on the plains as is, they don't need a Crinos form to get that job done.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one I actually almost entirely agree with you on. Initially the Ajaba were just put out just to be antagonists to the Bastet. Their concept has undergone some of the biggest changes edition to edition and I think overall that was to their detriment. They basically come across as Garou-lite now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062278#post1062278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Breed should only exist if there is a genuine need for it which cannot be fulfilled by regular nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as? (which ones do you think fail that test)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062278#post1062278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OR, alternatively, each Breed being given a purpose by Gaia is just lore that the Breeds made up as part of their religions and various cults, and they're just a spiritual phenomena which exists without any divine purpose... which would explain why the Lore has gaps and holes in it</div> </div> </div> </div>It's too early for this The-whole-spiritual-world-is-a-conspriracy line of thought you keep pushing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062282#post1062282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for a Breed I'd be interested in seeing...<br /> <br /> Werebirds. I feel like Corax are a tad restrictive, and it would be nice if they got a Bastet treatment and you could be a Falcon, Eagle, Owl, all with slight shifts in purpose. All of them are messengers, but get slightly different Forms and Gifts. So only Ravens get the Eye-Eating power, but Falcons get some combat powers from the Garou lists and Owls get some healing powers from the Gurahl lists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I would go full ahead with making various avian species into Fera, but I do remember something about either Falcon or Eagle Changers being mentioned somewhere. I was going to get around to doing an Eagle writeup and have them be Helios' warriors (counterpart to the Garou) who were killed early on because the Garou didn't want competition. And with only 1 warrior race left, the Garou become the defacto warriors for all of Gaia.<br /> If you were to go the various species route, then it would seem to be easier to just spread them out similar to Auspices, with the Owls being stealth types (Ragabash), the Ravens basically filling the Galliard role. That leaves you Falcons and Eagles. So maybe Philodox and Ahrouns respectively. With Theurge type powers spread throughout the 4.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062282#post1062282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would also make the Messengers global, since Ravens aren't a 100% globalized species but &quot;birds&quot; are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Camazotz were supposed to fill in the rest of the world along with the Ravens. So there is that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062282#post1062282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wereinsects are something I want to want, but cannot actually see being cool. Werespiders are enough, and I'm glad that the Werebees were hounded to extinction in the Insect War.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of insect races never really interested me. I agree that the Ananasi seem to be fine as the only ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062282#post1062282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wereapes is something that will never work since humans are so close to Apes as is. Same issue with Monkeys and other &quot;close&quot; relatives, since the point of Werewolf is being kin to something distinctly inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. There could be something interesting about having Wereapes. The Yeren got a pretty decent writeup. Just not sure what their role would be.<br /> <br /> Given the small range or Gorillas, I would be inclined to add them to my Gaia's personality aspects idea and have them be the race that was tucked away in Africa (I wanted one for each continent). And the Wyrm's perversion of the race would help account for why the Yeren as so far ahead of the other Mockery breeds for accomplishments. Maybe Pentex unknowingly stumbled across Gorilla-Changer kin for use in their programs.<br /> /shrug<br /> It's early and these are all pre-coffee thoughts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T08:09:05-07:00","id":1062305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062301#post1062301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eh. most or all of the breeds were put out at the same time (Player's Handbook). The Breed books later on just vastly expanded on each (except for the Nuwisha one that got a horribly short page count).<br /> <br /> <br /> This one I actually almost entirely agree with you on. Initially the Ajaba were just put out just to be antagonists to the Bastet. Their concept has undergone some of the biggest changes edition to edition and I think overall that was to their detriment. They basically come across as Garou-lite now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Such as? (which ones do you think fail that test)<br /> <br /> <br /> It's too early for this The-whole-spiritual-world-is-a-conspriracy line of thought you keep pushing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know if I would go full ahead with making various avian species into Fera, but I do remember something about either Falcon or Eagle Changers being mentioned somewhere. I was going to get around to doing an Eagle writeup and have them be Helios' warriors (counterpart to the Garou) who were killed early on because the Garou didn't want competition. And with only 1 warrior race left, the Garou become the defacto warriors for all of Gaia.<br /> If you were to go the various species route, then it would seem to be easier to just spread them out similar to Auspices, with the Owls being stealth types (Ragabash), the Ravens basically filling the Galliard role. That leaves you Falcons and Eagles. So maybe Philodox and Ahrouns respectively. With Theurge type powers spread throughout the 4.<br /> <br /> Well the Camazotz were supposed to fill in the rest of the world along with the Ravens. So there is that.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea of insect races never really interested me. I agree that the Ananasi seem to be fine as the only ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eh. There could be something interesting about having Wereapes. The Yeren got a pretty decent writeup. Just not sure what their role would be.<br /> <br /> Given the small range or Gorillas, I would be inclined to add them to my Gaia's personality aspects idea and have them be the race that was tucked away in Africa (I wanted one for each continent). And the Wyrm's perversion of the race would help account for why the Yeren as so far ahead of the other Mockery breeds for accomplishments. Maybe Pentex unknowingly stumbled across Gorilla-Changer kin for use in their programs.<br /> /shrug<br /> It's early and these are all pre-coffee thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>- The Hyenas fail the test since their role is carried out by normal nature, and the Ratkin if necessary. The Foxes... don't really seem to have a singular role, and their backstory even confronts this, but it isn't all that fulfilling. The Mokole seem a bit odd, since every Breed has a spiritual memory and ancestor memory, and the role of &quot;Gaia's Memory&quot; could easily be fulfilled by a spiritual entity, there isn't any need for a physical presence in the world. I love the Mokole but I think they need a new purpose... perhaps they were the Garou of the Dinosaur Age? They're a spiritual hangover from a primordial past, usurped from their position, looking to recover the Dragon form (stolen from them in a battle with the Garou, who wounded Dragon) and reclaim the role of Gaia's Warriors.<br /> <br /> - Well the &quot;it's all a lie&quot; bit does cover up any logical issues with the roles of the breeds, but I do mention in the post that it's not a very fulfilling response at most tables.<br /> <br /> - I'm aware of the Camazotz, but having an entirely different breed to fill in a geographical gap is a bit odd to me when you could just have a type of Corvid filling in that space and give Bats a different role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T08:29:40-07:00","id":1062312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062305#post1062305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - The Hyenas fail the test since their role is carried out by normal nature, and the Ratkin if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062305#post1062305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Foxes... don't really seem to have a singular role, and their backstory even confronts this, but it isn't all that fulfilling.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have a purpose, but it isn't terribly clear and is somewhat hidden in their book. They basically amount to civilization assassins. They bring down empires. I can see why late in the game it was decided that Gaia needed something to try and counter the advancement of humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062305#post1062305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Mokole seem a bit odd, since every Breed has a spiritual memory and ancestor memory, and the role of &quot;Gaia's Memory&quot; could easily be fulfilled by a spiritual entity, there isn't any need for a physical presence in the world. I love the Mokole but I think they need a new purpose... perhaps they were the Garou of the Dinosaur Age? They're a spiritual hangover from a primordial past, usurped from their position, looking to recover the Dragon form (stolen from them in a battle with the Garou, who wounded Dragon) and reclaim the role of Gaia's Warriors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree entirely here. No other breed comes close to doing the job the Mokole do as the memory. And it might be worth reading Shattered Dreams. There is a section on the Dragon Kings and their role in the past. They weren't anywhere close to the &quot;Garou of the Dinosaur Age&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062305#post1062305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - Well the &quot;it's all a lie&quot; bit does cover up any logical issues with the roles of the breeds, but I do mention in the post that it's not a very fulfilling response at most tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet it keeps coming up thread after thread. Either way, this isn't worth getting hung up on in this thread since it has nothing to do with the current topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062305#post1062305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - I'm aware of the Camazotz, but having an entirely different breed to fill in a geographical gap is a bit odd to me when you could just have a type of Corvid filling in that space and give Bats a different role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the format of basically having Helio's messengers (Corax) and Luna's messengers (Camazotz). It sets up an interesting dynamic to me, where the 2 more prominent Celestines had a hand in their own Fera created. We don't have a similar setup with any of the other breeds. And it's actually based off of this relationship that I grew fonder on the idea of Eagles (maybe Falcons, to tie in Horus' visage) as Helio's warriors.<br /> I can see why you think they might be redundant, but neither Breed covers the world enough to do the job themselves, which is something you've already pointed out as a flaw. But there just aren't going to be any animal breeds that span the world enough to do any real worldwide job outside of rats and spiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T08:42:52-07:00","id":1062314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062288#post1062288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's much closer to a standard Fera. I like it.<br /> For roles, how is the Joy of Gaia different from the Laughter of Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction is that the Laughter of the Nuwisha is a cold, cynical one that FORCES you to &quot;deal with it&quot; and accept the cruelty and ugliness of the world without an ounce of warmth or compassion, the &quot;Joy&quot; that the Encantado bring is a warm and healing one that reminds the Warriors WHY they are fighting.<br /> <br /> Whereas Samwise Gamgee answered the weary and suicidal Frodo's &quot;What are we holding onto, Sam&quot; with &quot;That there's GOOD left in this World, Mr Frodo, and it's worth fighting for&quot;, a disgusting cynical New York &quot;comedian&quot; smartass like Jerry Seinfeld would slap Frodo across the head and sneer &quot;Get the hell up, nobody cares! Every mother should stand over an open grave and push their children into it for all it's worth! There's no meaning to anything anyways; yadda yadda blah blah irony and cynicism makes me smarter than people with Kindness, Heart and Humanity; I spit on your tears!&quot;<br /> <br /> Encantado Were-Dolphins are the Warm-And-Kind Samwise Gamgees that hug you and give you Hope in your darkest hour, Nuwisha are the smartass Jerry Seinfelds who kick you while you're crying and FORCE you to laugh along with it.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that the Joy and Laughter that Encantado bring would make them bosom-friends with the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia and The Fianna. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062288#post1062288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On forms, I would drop the blowhole in homid, since Homid form is literally just supposed to be human form. I don't know that they need a Glabro, but if you give them one I would start with the blowhole concept there. And since that's a near human form, you can have the blowhole between the shoulder blades so as to not deal with the idea that there's an airway going up through the head of a mostly humanoid form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, come to think about, that would make more logical sense. Sorry, just found South American Mythology so refreshingly original that I couldn't resist refrencing it. Okay, OUT goes the Blow-Hole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062288#post1062288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hadn't heard that. Kind of funny that they then went and made Rokea fairly sexually aggressive once they come on land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr Skemp's concerns are odd considering that later editions openly admit that the sadly-large Fianna Metis population is PRECISELY because those child-abandoning Celtic hypocrites ARE promiscuous whore-mongers with sex-drives that would put Casanova-himself to shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 03-14-2017, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:09:53-07:00","id":1062323,"title":"","content":"That makes the role of the Foxes VERY similar to the Ratkin and the Weresnakes. The problem is when the roles start to overlap and things feel... clustered. Very clustered. Here's my list, for posterity:<br /> <br /> Garou: Land Warriors<br /> <br /> Gurahl: Guides and Healers of Gaia's Children<br /> <br /> Apis: Guides for primitive humanity (failed in their role)<br /> <br /> Nagah: Assassins<br /> <br /> Nuwisha: Teachers. Used to be a global species, War of Rage changed that.<br /> <br /> Kitsune: Guides for civilized humanity (hence their late arrival)<br /> <br /> Grondr: Groomers, remove subtle wyrm taint and keep natural landscape in harmony (lacked a Crinos form, why would they even need one after all, and so were readily slaughtered)<br /> <br /> Ratkin: Population Control (Camazotz are a relative and hold the same purpose, along with a spiritual/biological ancestry in common)<br /> <br /> Mokole: The precursors to the Garou (yes, this is a change, I'm aware that they aren't &quot;prehistoric Garou&quot;, I'm saying that it would make more sense if they were)<br /> <br /> Corax: Messengers<br /> <br /> Some other Bird Group: Sky Warriors<br /> <br /> Rokea: Sea Warriors<br /> <br /> Bastet: Information Gatherers... feels off. Firstly we have the Corax who are Messengers, and so we sort of assume that the Corax are good at collecting information. Secondly we have Lions. When we think of Lions, Jaguars, Cougars, even housecats... we don't really think of spies as our first thought. We could call them Leaders, and say that Gaia's intent was for the Bastet to rule over the other Changing Breeds and coordinate their roles. Due to fault in both the Bastet and the Garou, this fell apart and was one element of the War of Rage's origin. I'll say &quot;Intended Rulers&quot;, since Cat played hard-to-get and wouldn't have accepted a lesser role. Plus Cats are naturally regal animals.<br /> <br /> Ajaba: Not a thing. There's no reason for them to be a thing, unless they're given a new role.<br /> <br /> Ananasi are supposed to be an abnormality, since they are the only non-Gaian breed (lets just ignore the frogs and roaches, shall we?) and so them covering every role is fine in my opinion. It reeks a little bit of &quot;oh, you think this splat is good? Well THIS splat sees a much bigger picture, and uses the other Splat as pawns&quot;, the sort of thing that made Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand unpopular, but it's also weirdly realistic since spiders are so universal and so subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-14-2017, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:46:18-07:00","id":1062345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062314#post1062314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, come to think about, that would make more logical sense. Sorry, just found South American Mythology so refreshingly original that I couldn't resist refrencing it. Okay, OUT goes the Blow-Hole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rokea had similar with the mouth between the shoulder blades myth. You can add the blowhole in homid as a Gift to keep the inspiration/flavor of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062323#post1062323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That makes the role of the Foxes VERY similar to the Ratkin and the Weresnakes. The problem is when the roles start to overlap and things feel... clustered. Very clustered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar, though not the same as the Ratkin. But considering the Ratkin had failed their purpose by that point, there is something to be said for a new Breed being brought in, who are better at navigating sociopolitical environments as opposed to just having tools to mitigate numbers. And The Nagah do something entirely different so I'm not sure how you see overlap there. The Nagah solely judge Fera and their fulfilling of their jobs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062323#post1062323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my list, for posterity:<br /> Garou: Land Warriors<br /> <br /> Gurahl: Guides and Healers of Gaia's Children<br /> <br /> Apis: Guides for primitive humanity (failed in their role)<br /> <br /> Nagah: Assassins<br /> <br /> Nuwisha: Teachers. Used to be a global species, War of Rage changed that.<br /> <br /> Kitsune: Guides for civilized humanity (hence their late arrival)<br /> <br /> Grondr: Groomers, remove subtle wyrm taint and keep natural landscape in harmony (lacked a Crinos form, why would they even need one after all, and so were readily slaughtered)<br /> <br /> Ratkin: Population Control (Camazotz are a relative and hold the same purpose, along with a spiritual/biological ancestry in common)<br /> <br /> Mokole: The precursors to the Garou (yes, this is a change, I'm aware that they aren't &quot;prehistoric Garou&quot;, I'm saying that it would make more sense if they were)<br /> <br /> Corax: Messengers<br /> <br /> Some other Bird Group: Sky Warriors<br /> <br /> Rokea: Sea Warriors<br /> <br /> Bastet: Information Gatherers... feels off. Firstly we have the Corax who are Messengers, and so we sort of assume that the Corax are good at collecting information. Secondly we have Lions. When we think of Lions, Jaguars, Cougars, even housecats... we don't really think of spies as our first thought. We could call them Leaders, and say that Gaia's intent was for the Bastet to rule over the other Changing Breeds and coordinate their roles. Due to fault in both the Bastet and the Garou, this fell apart and was one element of the War of Rage's origin. I'll say &quot;Intended Rulers&quot;, since Cat played hard-to-get and wouldn't have accepted a lesser role. Plus Cats are naturally regal animals.<br /> <br /> Ajaba: Not a thing. There's no reason for them to be a thing, unless they're given a new role.<br /> <br /> Ananasi are supposed to be an abnormality, since they are the only non-Gaian breed (lets just ignore the frogs and roaches, shall we?) and so them covering every role is fine in my opinion. It reeks a little bit of &quot;oh, you think this splat is good? Well THIS splat sees a much bigger picture, and uses the other Splat as pawns&quot;, the sort of thing that made Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand unpopular, but it's also weirdly realistic since spiders are so universal and so subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your list is...odd. You don't want overlap, but you have &quot;Guides&quot; (3 times) and &quot;Teachers&quot;. Is there a difference? Why does Gaia need an &quot;Assassin&quot; Breed (and does having one mean the Rakin lose Knife Skulkers since they're now redundant)? I think your list is just as arbitrary as the canon list, if not moreso. Out of you 13 Gaian Changers, 4 of them have the role of &quot;warrior&quot; and 4 of them are teachers of guides. So really, 2/3 of you list seem to fill just 2 roles. After those, you just have Assassins (again, why?), Groomers (No Crinos), Population Control (which also wouldn't need Crinos by your logic) and Messengers (again, wouldn't need a Crinos) and Information Gatherers (which you argue should be part of the Messenger role). And really, none of the &quot;Guide/Teacher&quot; roles need Crinos either.<br /> <br /> So if your reorganizing doesn't really fix anything (it doesn't seem to), then it seems questionable to put the work in.<br /> <br /> And again, I agree some of the Fera (Ajaba in particular) need role clarifications. But your approach doesn't actually do anything for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T10:32:24-07:00","id":1062363,"title":"","content":"More focused back on topic:<br /> Falcon Changers (I think I decided on since falcons over eagles since they seem to have a greater range)<br /> Helios' Warriors<br /> Vulnerable to Gold (No Silver weakness)<br /> 3 Forms:<br /> Crinos: Str+3/Dex+3/Stam+3 and Flight<br /> Avian: Dex+4, Per+2<br /> (if I were to include eagles, I would just modify the stats by -1 Dex and +1 Str)<br /> <br /> Their Crinos stats don't match their animal stat inspirations because they don't have to. The strength bonus is really just about them being warriors.<br /> <br /> Rage based on Auspice (2, 3 or 4)<br /> Auspices: Spiritualists (Theurge), Judges (Philodox) and Fighters (Ahroun)<br /> Homid: Gnosis 2, Willpower 5<br /> Avian: Gnosis 4, Willpower 3<br /> <br /> The falcons would lack solid defensive Gifts but have a variety of Gifts to assist in hit and run tactics.<br /> After the Breed's destruction at the hands of the Garou, Falcon (the totem) stepped in to claim one of the newly emerging Tribes as his own (this assumed the Garou destroyed Falcon-changers prior to the Tribes forming obviously).<br /> <br /> If this idea was expanded to more bird species, I would have Owls with night and Umbra (including the Dark Umbra) oriented Gifts, Falcons with leadership and judgement Gifts, Eagles with the most combat focused Gifts. Hawks, falcons and eagles seem to hold some similar places in overall mythologies so I'm not sure where I would put hawks in all of this.<br /> <br /> It's far from a fully formed idea, but it's a start.<br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:37:48-07:00","id":1062395,"title":"","content":"I think that I would prefer the introduction of an Owl Fera. The Owl Fera would serve as the Warriors of the Air and the Warrior of the Night (as the Camazotz served as the secret messengers of Gaia). They would be capable of traveling into the Umbra by walking into the shadows, similar to the Camazotz.<br /> <br /> Since owls are silent predators, I would give them a -2 difficulty modifier to Stealth. I would give them forms similar to that of the Camazotz, though I would increase the Strength and Stamina of their forms by one each because owls are much stronger and tougher than bats. I would also give them Rage 1, Gnosis 5, and Willpower 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 03-14-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:47:12-07:00","id":1062404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062345#post1062345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar, though not the same as the Ratkin. But considering the Ratkin had failed their purpose by that point, there is something to be said for a new Breed being brought in, who are better at navigating sociopolitical environments as opposed to just having tools to mitigate numbers. And The Nagah do something entirely different so I'm not sure how you see overlap there. The Nagah solely judge Fera and their fulfilling of their jobs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your list is...odd. You don't want overlap, but you have &quot;Guides&quot; (3 times) and &quot;Teachers&quot;. Is there a difference? Why does Gaia need an &quot;Assassin&quot; Breed (and does having one mean the Rakin lose Knife Skulkers since they're now redundant)? I think your list is just as arbitrary as the canon list, if not moreso. Out of you 13 Gaian Changers, 4 of them have the role of &quot;warrior&quot; and 4 of them are teachers of guides. So really, 2/3 of you list seem to fill just 2 roles. After those, you just have Assassins (again, why?), Groomers (No Crinos), Population Control (which also wouldn't need Crinos by your logic) and Messengers (again, wouldn't need a Crinos) and Information Gatherers (which you argue should be part of the Messenger role). And really, none of the &quot;Guide/Teacher&quot; roles need Crinos either.<br /> <br /> So if your reorganizing doesn't really fix anything (it doesn't seem to), then it seems questionable to put the work in.<br /> <br /> And again, I agree some of the Fera (Ajaba in particular) need role clarifications. But your approach doesn't actually do anything for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>My list has 3 types of warriors which are specifically delineated in their placement. My list also has three kinds of Guides which have specific roles and do their own thing.<br /> <br /> The Ratkin need a Crinos since population control sometimes means killing. Same with the Guides, as occasionally a Bear or Fox or Coyote will need to fight to defend a student. I simply can't see &quot;Gaia's garbage-men&quot; needing to fight, ever. They're roaming the plains eating up Bad Things like rotting corrupted environments and keeping balance in the biosphere, which is a role which needs Intelligence (justifying a Boar and Human form) but doesn't necessitate fighting. You could make them Groomers and Guardians of Caerns (justifying the Crinos), and that would explain why they were wiped out, since other Breeds would covet Cairns and this would lead to their downfall.<br /> <br /> Gaia needs Assassins since sometimes a threat needs to be neutralized stealthily, and the Snakes excel in subtlety. Fomori and Armies of Spiral Dancers? Garou. A single powerful Bastet who has become corrupted by power? Sometimes a Snake will do the job better. And when I call the Snakes &quot;assassins&quot;, I do understand that they kill Fera, and &quot;Assassins&quot; is an over-simplification of their role, correct.<br /> <br /> Guides /=/ Teachers. A Guide tells you what to do and pushes you in the right direction. An Apis might teach traditions to a tribe which make them revere animals, and keep them in line with a Gaian lifestyle. They might teach them to accept travellers and feed them, making things easier for Homid Kinfolk, and they might teach them to leave offerings to animals (for non-Homids).<br /> <br /> The Nuwisha, on the other hand, would be teaching Fera Gifts and Abilities specifically. Their role would be that of a Mentor to any Fera they thought was worth their time. How does this differ from the Gurahl? They'd be spiritual advisers and sources of inspiration, and they aren't teaching Gifts to outsiders except in exceptional circumstances since teaching isn't their role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:08:09-07:00","id":1062571,"title":"","content":"Breed: Were-Squirrels<br /> Job: Gather lost relics and return the spirits of lost fetishes back to natural state.<br /> Vulnerability: Little People Homid Form / War-form normal short size / Animal form of a squirrel (Reduced health levels -0 -1 -2 -4 Incap )<br /> Special Abilities: Gifts towards theft and escape. Gifts that allow bypass barriers.Gifts on locating items with spirits. Rites on undoing fetishes.<br /> <br /> These people are unlike any other of Gaia's children. She chose them for the small size which allow them to move unseen. They live nearly always in the Preumbra instead of the normal world. As a people they don't relate to the humans of the world but those creatures of the Umbra. Since their birth they have been quite and moving from place to place but since the recent time they have been charge with bring back those spirits who have been made into fetishes that have been forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":3293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","user":"Rahod","date":". 03-15-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T12:47:08-07:00","id":1062927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062571#post1062571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breed: Were-Squirrels<br /> Job: Gather lost relics and return the spirits of lost fetishes back to natural state.<br /> Vulnerability: Little People Homid Form / War-form normal short size / Animal form of a squirrel (Reduced health levels -0 -1 -2 -4 Incap )<br /> Special Abilities: Gifts towards theft and escape. Gifts that allow bypass barriers.Gifts on locating items with spirits. Rites on undoing fetishes.<br /> <br /> These people are unlike any other of Gaia's children. She chose them for the small size which allow them to move unseen. They live nearly always in the Preumbra instead of the normal world. As a people they don't relate to the humans of the world but those creatures of the Umbra. Since their birth they have been quite and moving from place to place but since the recent time they have been charge with bring back those spirits who have been made into fetishes that have been forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is an interesting concept. It's a unique role that doesn't really have any crossover with established Fera. I don't know that it is entirely necessary, but that isn't so much the point of this thread.<br /> <br /> The animal form reduced health levels thing is a bit out of place since that isn't generally how animal forms work. That is better represented by taking a hit to Stamina (thus soaking less), but even that I wouldn't do since neither Ratkin or Corax suffer that in their small animal forms (and Ratkin actually get a bonus). I always chalked it up to the animals forms being somewhat supernaturally resilient.<br /> <br /> I would assume they have some sort of Breed immunity from suffering Disconnection. Are you picturing them with a Silver vulnerability or gold (and why)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:02:20-07:00","id":1063009,"title":"","content":"I see your point on the health factor, Yes they do not have to worry about Disconnection, and on the point of gold over silver I just thought they would be aligned with sun more than the moon since the breed it self is not very nocturnal. But if you wanted more story line behind it i would say they believe that Helios guides them by shining the light on that which has been lost while Luna hide them in the shadows of the night. You could even give them a form of ADD/ADHD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://orig06.deviantart.net/be80/f/2007/227/c/7/weresquirrel_by_darknatasha.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orig06.deviantart.net/be80/f/2007/227/c/7/weresquirrel_by_darknatasha.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orig06.deviantart.net/be80/f/2007/227/c/7/weresquirrel_by_darknatasha.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://orig06.deviantart.net/be80/f/2007/227/c/7/weresquirrel_by_darknatasha.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":3293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","user":"Rahod","date":". 03-15-2017, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:57:15-07:00","id":1063055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062927#post1062927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is an interesting concept. It's a unique role that doesn't really have any crossover with established Fera. I don't know that it is entirely necessary, but that isn't so much the point of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be necessary if it were written in a way that made it necessary... squirrels IRL forget where they buried stuff all the time (or they are eaten before they can come back to their cache). Maybe were-squirrels originally were the safekeepers of fetishes large and small, hiding them away for safekeeping and then allowing them to be found only by those who were truly worthy.<br /> <br /> Then something goes wrong.<br /> <br /> Maybe the squirrels get complacent, or maybe when they refuse a Garou warlord things go south. Maybe the Bastet, charged as they are with watching over the umbral places, think they would make better keepers of the spirit-infused items. Regardless, during the War of Rage a bunch of squirrel-folk were slaughtered but they took their secrets to their graves and their many hiding places were lost to the ages. Now the descendants of the squirrel fera scour the Tellurian for the locations of these lost dormant fetishes. Assuming they succeed, will they give them to the fera who wronged them in ages past... or use these terrible weapons themselves to seek revenge?<br /> <br /> p.s. I like the idea of killer squirrels.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T21:16:03-07:00","id":1063113,"title":"","content":"I would think that Were-Squirrels would be something like Grace out of El Goonish Shive, though that would probably make them capable of taking out groups of experienced Garou without breaking a sweat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T21:57:44-07:00","id":1063123,"title":"","content":"Are the Weresquirrels anything like these fellas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Chip is SO Awesome with that Indian Jones Hat!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRMgnu5jvvZVnNfXR7xcGy7ym3QSXz7xRrZbRHTcTqvbJG5ECis\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> And a recommended Name for the Were-Squirrels?<br /> The <i>Aeschyli</i> (Literally Latin For Squirrel) or <i>Song-Shu</i> for the Taiwanese Sub-Breed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Keep Up The Good Work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 03-16-2017, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T23:25:29-07:00","id":1063131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1063123#post1063123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Weresquirrels anything like these fellas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Chip is SO Awesome with that Indian Jones Hat!<br /> <br /> And a recommended Name for the Were-Squirrels?<br /> The <i>Aeschyli</i> (Literally Latin For Squirrel) or <i>Song-Shu</i> for the Taiwanese Sub-Breed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Keep Up The Good Work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I loved Chip so much when I was younger. Never really watched the show, just had an action figure I loved to death for some reason. I almost mentioned Indy in my earlier post, I think there could be parallels made between the adventures of the courageous squirrels and everybody's favorite Nazi-punching prof. <br /> <br /> I think the Aeschyli name sounds awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T12:16:25-07:00","id":1063363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1063009#post1063009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point on the health factor, Yes they do not have to worry about Disconnection, and on the point of gold over silver I just thought they would be aligned with sun more than the moon since the breed it self is not very nocturnal. But if you wanted more story line behind it i would say they believe that Helios guides them by shining the light on that which has been lost while Luna hide them in the shadows of the night. You could even give them a form of ADD/ADHD.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orig06.deviantart.net/be80/f/2007/227/c/7/weresquirrel_by_darknatasha.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://orig06.deviantart.net/be80/f/...arknatasha.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of them being associated with Helios.<br /> <br /> Now trying to figure out what to do with their form stats to differentiate them at least somewhat from the Ratkin stats. I'm thinking maybe taking a dot or 2 from Stamina and adding it to Perception since the Aeschyli (I also like this name) will be tasked with finding things. There is also the possibility of not hitting their social traits so hard in Crinos/animal forms.<br /> <br /> So maybe something like:<br /> Crinos: Str+1/Dex+4/Stam+1, Man -1, Per+2<br /> Note: Keeps Appearance score (like Kitsune)<br /> Squirrel: Str-1/Dex+3/Stam+0, Man -1, Per+3<br /> <br /> And like Ratatosk, the clever squirrel totem (Get book), they only enter Fox Frenzy.<br /> Starting Rage/Gnosis/Will:<br /> Homid - 1/2/4<br /> Animal - 1/5/3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-16-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T14:46:55-07:00","id":1063528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1063363#post1063363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of them being associated with Helios.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GaN7BHijXIA\" target=\"_blank\">In your face, Luna!</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now trying to figure out what to do with their form stats to differentiate them at least somewhat from the Ratkin stats. I'm thinking maybe taking a dot or 2 from Stamina and adding it to Perception since the Aeschyli (I also like this name) will be tasked with finding things. There is also the possibility of not hitting their social traits so hard in Crinos/animal forms.<br /> <br /> So maybe something like:<br /> Crinos: Str+1/Dex+4/Stam+1, Man -1, Per+2<br /> Note: Keeps Appearance score (like Kitsune) </div> </div> </div>That just makes me think of Makoto even more. Maybe go back to the frightening-ass squirrel beast posted up-thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:14:46-07:00","id":1063668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1063528#post1063528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GaN7BHijXIA\" target=\"_blank\">In your face, Luna!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Haha! I've never heard of this game and so had no idea what to expect when I clicked this link. That's too funny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1063528#post1063528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That just makes me think of Makoto even more. Maybe go back to the frightening-ass squirrel beast posted up-thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I just couldn't really justify more physical dots and the lack of an App 0 helps to balance it a bit. I could see her form as a partial change thing or as a separate form Gift. Doesn't matter much since I don't think any of us are taking this terribly seriously. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:14:46-07:00","id":1064949,"title":"","content":"So to sum up so far, we have:<br /> Koalas: Imagination of Gaia<br /> River Dolphins: Joy of Gaia<br /> Horses: Gaia's Celestial Heralds<br /> Falcons: Helios' Warriors<br /> Squirrels: Finders of the Lost<br /> <br /> I still want to write up Gorillas, but I'm drawing a blank on what their role should be. It has to be a specialized one that doesn't require them to go around the world. So I'm thinking something like the Nuwisha (Laughter) or the River Dolphins (Joy) or the Koalas (Imagination). Something vague that is important to Gaia's survival but can be hidden away until needed (probably after or during the Apocalypse). And I would say some sort of purpose that the Wyrm/Pentex has perverted to &quot;create&quot; the Yeren (in this scenario, the Yeren are the fallen version of this Fera type).<br /> <br /> Any ideas?<br /> Balancing form stats system-wise will be easy enough and can be done afterwards (I'm short on time atm).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T21:29:34-07:00","id":1065088,"title":"","content":"Would these be good examples of what the Crinos forms of the proposed Were-Birds (namely WereRooster and WereBlackSwan) would <i>roughly</i> look like? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a0/Foghorn_Leghorn.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <img src=\"http://cartoonbros.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/daffy-duck-8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:26:45-07:00","id":1065360,"title":"","content":"Well with the Pentex mockery breed Yeren I wouldn't go with Gorillas but maybe monkeys and maybe they can be teachers of tools aka Fetish Crafters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:25:16-07:00","id":1065391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1065360#post1065360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well with the Pentex mockery breed Yeren I wouldn't go with Gorillas but maybe monkeys and maybe they can be teachers of tools aka Fetish Crafters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like the idea of the Yeren being the bastardization of a long dead Fera breed. It would go a ways towards explaining why the Yeren have been so successful in developing Rank and Gifts (compared to the other Mockery Breeds). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:00:33-07:00","id":1067964,"title":"","content":"With Falcons as Sky Warriors, they could learn the Corax's offensive gifts but at 1 level lower; so the level 3 Corax gift with a deadly feather dart would be a level 2 gift for them.<br /> <br /> I think it would make sense if they could Swoop Sideways; they can dive into water (reflective) and enter the Umbra through that, in the fashion that birds of prey dive to grab fish.<br /> <br /> However, Corax aren't just Ravens, they're Corvids. Wouldn't it be better to have our 'Falcons' be a larger family which contains multiple birds of prey? That way they are global and allow for more player customisation, like playing as a jaguar or lion or cougar.<br /> <br /> Also, the Vultures are a tribe of the &quot;Falcon&quot; Breed which fell to the Wyrm, much in the way that the Skull Pigs and Spiral Dancers have. They give air support to Hives and they dream of the Wyrm consuming the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-25-2017, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T09:33:27-07:00","id":1068026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1067964#post1067964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With Falcons as Sky Warriors, they could learn the Corax's offensive gifts but at 1 level lower; so the level 3 Corax gift with a deadly feather dart would be a level 2 gift for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds feasible. The only 2 Gifts off the top of my head that fall into this category though would be Hummingbird Dart and Razorfeathers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1067964#post1067964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it would make sense if they could Swoop Sideways; they can dive into water (reflective) and enter the Umbra through that, in the fashion that birds of prey dive to grab fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe all falcons dive into the water, though requiring them to dive might be a thing. And have a Gift to step sideways normally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1067964#post1067964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, Corax aren't just Ravens, they're Corvids. Wouldn't it be better to have our 'Falcons' be a larger family which contains multiple birds of prey? That way they are global and allow for more player customisation, like playing as a jaguar or lion or cougar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Corax are just ravens (in general). The idea of expanding them into other corvids is fine, but all of the books always presented them as being just ravens. The breed and form sections support this (specifically calling them out as not being crows).<br /> That being said, I do actually like the idea of various raptor changers. You could have falcons, hawks (not sure how much different thematically they would be from falcons), eagles, vultures (possibly fallen, though they'd need an uncorrupted purpose to start). Owls also fit into this category, but not really with the theme of Helios' brood.<br /> <br /> I could see the different types of raptors as being different Tribes (like the Bastet examples you give).<br /> In that setup, you could have:<br /> Eagles: Warriors<br /> Falcons: Royalty/Leaders<br /> Hawks: ? (most myths I found had falcons and hawks in the same roles)<br /> Vultures: ?<br /> Owls (if included): Umbral travelers<br /> <br /> The other raptors I can think of that aren't in the above groups are: the Osprey, Secretarybird and Kites.<br /> I suppose kites can be lumped in with hawks. If we eliminate Owls from this, we can move their Umbral role over to hawks and/or kites maybe.<br /> Still not sure where the Osprey and Secretarybird would end up thematically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1067964#post1067964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, the Vultures are a tribe of the &quot;Falcon&quot; Breed which fell to the Wyrm, much in the way that the Skull Pigs and Spiral Dancers have. They give air support to Hives and they dream of the Wyrm consuming the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Addressed above, but yea this idea makes sense. They just need to have had something to do prior to falling to the Wyrm. Maybe they were in charge of finding the Wyrm to fight? And them falling could have lead to the rest of the Breed getting slaughtered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T09:58:57-07:00","id":1068028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1068026#post1068026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Corax are just ravens (in general). The idea of expanding them into other corvids is fine, but all of the books always presented them as being just ravens. The breed and form sections support this (specifically calling them out as not being crows).</div> </div> </div> </div>For really bad reasons that don't make sense, because all corvids are actually quite bright, and the earlier research on corvid tool use and self-motivated simple tool fabrication comes from New Caledonian crows. Also, in other locations, the breed is explicitly called out as not being ravens, such as in Africa, where they're white-necked crows and likely others. Also, there are no common ravens (<i>Corvus corax</i>) commonly found in Tengu skies. Carrion crows would be more common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-25-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T10:45:00-07:00","id":1068041,"title":"","content":"Well I'd argue that they should all be Warriors of a kind, just ones who fight in different ways.<br /> <br /> Vultures: They hide and wait for a foe to be weak before striking. They are slow but efficient. A Vulture might bother a Fomori frequently to stop it from getting drinkable water, and slowly as the thirst takes over they take advantage of this weakness. Their Gifts would include an artificially forced Hunger/Thirst/Exhaustion state which they can use to strike a foe at their weakest. Their Crinos form gives extra Stamina to help them Bother foes without risking death or exhaustion. They can't swoop sideways since they lost their connection to the Umbra when they moved away from water. They can step sideways with a gift. Their special ability is gaining power from those they consume, a quirk which led to their sad descent into the Wyrm's clutches.<br /> <br /> Eagles: These are larger birds, so they should be the most aggressive and confrontational Warriors, focusing on Gifts which give a heavy impact and are blunt attackers. Their Crinos gives extra Strength. While they can't keep up with Falcons their claws are crushing in Crinos and will end most lives efficiently. Their special ability is a sense of regality which has led to them becoming the leaders of the breed (along with their size); Leadership rolls are at -1 difficulty.<br /> <br /> Hawks: These are the best hunters. Their senses are unparalleled, and all Sensory rolls are made at an extra -1 difficulty compared to the other breeds. They have a level 1 gift which allows them to roll to pierce any type of invisibility or hiding power, difficulty determined by the level of the power (3 +level of power), where gaining successes equal to or greater than the power's activation breaks the effect.<br /> <br /> Falcons: These are smaller, and they are quick and deadly Warriors, focusing on Gifts which give them extra speed, agility and stealth. They travel the fastest and can pursue anything.<br /> <br /> Owls: Mystics who focus on strategy over raw strength. Their gifts give them a strong sense of how things look on both sides of the Gauntlet, so they make great observers and watchmen. They are very comfortable in the Umbra, cross over easily and fight well on the other side. Special feature is stepping sideways as an innate power.<br /> <br /> Their shared spirit is Bird of Prey, a powerful totem for all cannibalistic birds. They were sent to be the warriors of the sky because the Corax were so frail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:05:41-07:00","id":1068049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1068028#post1068028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For really bad reasons that don't make sense, because all corvids are actually quite bright, and the earlier research on corvid tool use and self-motivated simple tool fabrication comes from New Caledonian crows. Also, in other locations, the breed is explicitly called out as not being ravens, such as in Africa, where they're white-necked crows and likely others. Also, there are no common ravens (<i>Corvus corax</i>) commonly found in Tengu skies. Carrion crows would be more common.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Africa I was under the impression that they were <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-necked_raven\" target=\"_blank\">White-necked ravens</a>, not crows. I had to look it up but <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-necked_crow\" target=\"_blank\">white-necked crows </a>seem to only be found in the Caribbean.<br /> And for the Tengu, I would assume their Corvids are the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_crow\" target=\"_blank\">Jungle Crow</a>. Their range covers much of eastern Asia.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I actually do agree it doesn't necessarily make sense to limit them to Ravens, and to expand them to Corvids in general. But that isn't how the books treat them, for better or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:15:25-07:00","id":1068054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1068041#post1068041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I'd argue that they should all be Warriors of a kind, just ones who fight in different ways.<br /> <br /> Vultures: They hide and wait for a foe to be weak before striking. They are slow but efficient. A Vulture might bother a Fomori frequently to stop it from getting drinkable water, and slowly as the thirst takes over they take advantage of this weakness. Their Gifts would include an artificially forced Hunger/Thirst/Exhaustion state which they can use to strike a foe at their weakest. Their Crinos form gives extra Stamina to help them Bother foes without risking death or exhaustion. They can't swoop sideways since they lost their connection to the Umbra when they moved away from water. They can step sideways with a gift. Their special ability is gaining power from those they consume, a quirk which led to their sad descent into the Wyrm's clutches.<br /> <br /> Eagles: These are larger birds, so they should be the most aggressive and confrontational Warriors, focusing on Gifts which give a heavy impact and are blunt attackers. Their Crinos gives extra Strength. While they can't keep up with Falcons their claws are crushing in Crinos and will end most lives efficiently. Their special ability is a sense of regality which has led to them becoming the leaders of the breed (along with their size); Leadership rolls are at -1 difficulty.<br /> <br /> Hawks: These are the best hunters. Their senses are unparalleled, and all Sensory rolls are made at an extra -1 difficulty compared to the other breeds. They have a level 1 gift which allows them to roll to pierce any type of invisibility or hiding power, difficulty determined by the level of the power (3 +level of power), where gaining successes equal to or greater than the power's activation breaks the effect.<br /> <br /> Falcons: These are smaller, and they are quick and deadly Warriors, focusing on Gifts which give them extra speed, agility and stealth. They travel the fastest and can pursue anything.<br /> <br /> Owls: Mystics who focus on strategy over raw strength. Their gifts give them a strong sense of how things look on both sides of the Gauntlet, so they make great observers and watchmen. They are very comfortable in the Umbra, cross over easily and fight well on the other side. Special feature is stepping sideways as an innate power.<br /> <br /> Their shared spirit is Bird of Prey, a powerful totem for all cannibalistic birds. They were sent to be the warriors of the sky because the Corax were so frail.</div> </div> </div> </div>That all sounds pretty good. I was looking at the roles as being subroles of being Warriors (akin to the Garou Auspices covering general roles while all Garou are Warriors).<br /> <br /> I think I would drop the Owls and just focus on the diurnal raptors since we are starting with the premise (I am anyways) of these being Helios' Warriors. If you just want to go with &quot;Sky Warriors&quot; then that works fine.<br /> And within the WoD, Falcon is already known as a Totem of Leadership so I would err on the side of falcons (not eagles) being the born leaders among the raptors.<br /> <br /> I think our slightly different approaches are a result of my trying to tie it into the WoD as written already while you are rewriting the Fera as written. Not a big difference in the end, but it informs the result because of the different foundations we're starting with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T12:24:20-07:00","id":1068066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1068054#post1068054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all sounds pretty good. I was looking at the roles as being subroles of being Warriors (akin to the Garou Auspices covering general roles while all Garou are Warriors).<br /> <br /> I think I would drop the Owls and just focus on the diurnal raptors since we are starting with the premise (I am anyways) of these being Helios' Warriors. If you just want to go with &quot;Sky Warriors&quot; then that works fine.<br /> And within the WoD, Falcon is already known as a Totem of Leadership so I would err on the side of falcons (not eagles) being the born leaders among the raptors.<br /> <br /> I think our slightly different approaches are a result of my trying to tie it into the WoD as written already while you are rewriting the Fera as written. Not a big difference in the end, but it informs the result because of the different foundations we're starting with.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reasoning was that the guide of birds of prey I read described Eagles as regal, if there's established lore on Falcons as leaders... the issue for me is that Eagles are bigger and this means that they fit neatly as the leaders in a stereotypical sense.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if Owl would actually work. Might just be goofy. Since Hawks have such incredible senses, they could be the Umbra experts. Or, Luna wanted to get in on the fun and she made the Owl sub-breed, and there's a rivalry going on because Helios was big on the whole &quot;The birbs are mine&quot; thing. The Owls gained no support from the Corax and the other Birds during the War of Rage, and they were all but destroyed. The few survivors slumber in the Umbra, and seek the power to get revenge on their persecutors.<br /> <br /> When I get round to STing WTA, I'm going to completely redo the Fera's roles, remove a few breeds and change the Gift lists extensively. Corax just have so few gifts. I can't imagine playing one in a high EXP game, the list in the Changing Breeds book feels so bloody short and it feels incomplete... that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-25-2017, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T12:32:50-07:00","id":1068068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1068066#post1068066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I get round to STing WTA, I'm going to completely redo the Fera's roles, remove a few breeds and change the Gift lists extensively. Corax just have so few gifts. I can't imagine playing one in a high EXP game, the list in the Changing Breeds book feels so bloody short and it feels incomplete... that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Breed book doesn't do much to add to the list either. I think a lot of the problem is that Garou (being the main characters) get lots of support and so had a lot of Gifts added. The Fera generally seem to have a much smaller pool comparatively. The Cox and Nuwisha I think suffer the worst from this. I just look around the various books (Tribe books and Book of Auspices in particular) and let them have access to anything I feel is appropriate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:48:31-07:00","id":1068102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1068068#post1068068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Breed book doesn't do much to add to the list either. I think a lot of the problem is that Garou (being the main characters) get lots of support and so had a lot of Gifts added. The Fera generally seem to have a much smaller pool comparatively. The Cox and Nuwisha I think suffer the worst from this. I just look around the various books (Tribe books and Book of Auspices in particular) and let them have access to anything I feel is appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can't see a Squirrel Spirit being overly discerning. &quot;Wait! You aren't a member of this Arbitrary Group! No, I won't teach you how to do this thing that is kind of common to all animals in folklore, so there!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:51:03-07:00","id":1080710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1062261#post1062261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall way back when that Ethan Skemp said that the biggest problem with were-dolphins is that the species is rather sexually aggressive and this brought up a whole host of issues he didn't want to ever have to deal with. That said, the above idea is pretty cool. <br /> <br /> I, personally, want were-snails. Gaia's original messengers, until their failure to stop the first war of rage led to the job going to the Corax. <br /> <br /> (In all seriousness, as much as I enjoy all of the existing breeds, I would've preferred only having wolves, tigers, leopards, jaguars, hyena and sharks.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the fantasy series <i>Shadows of the Apt</i> by Adrian Tchaikovsky. It has slug-people in it, and they are basically walking gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:47:46-07:00","id":1085571,"title":"","content":"I think a were-porcupine would be pretty awesome, but I have no idea what their role would be.<br /> <br /> Slight off track, if Ananasi are Weaver creations, were-beavers could be Wyld creations. I know, you're probably thinking, beavers are builders and would be a Weaver creation. However, it's the beaver's dams that cause flooding, allowing trees and other life to flourish and add to a wild ecology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:11:40-07:00","id":1085613,"title":"","content":"Oh, and a Were-Moose sounds quite epic as well (just picture that crinos form). Again, no idea what their role would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:35:43-07:00","id":1085620,"title":"","content":"When I used to play on the White Wolf Unmoderated chats, there was a player who created a were-armadillo...she had them as defenders of sacred places. They guarded caerns/wallows/glens ect. as basically a breed of Caern Warders. She was fun to RP with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T18:15:26-07:00","id":1085638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AMmayhem</strong> <a